-- ccc1-s7-citizens-and-procedure.l4 -- section 7, subsections (4) to (7): Public Service employees abroad, sexual offences against children, trafficking in persons and
-- section 240.1 committed abroad by Canadian citizens and permanent residents; the consent of the Attorney General; where the proceedings are commenced and tried; the accused's appearance;
-- a person tried outside Canada; the consent of the Attorney General of Canada for an accused who is not a Canadian citizen.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- Shape as in the other section 7 modules: the lead-in is a scope limit (NOTHING outside it); an "if" ground that fails is JUST FALSE. A "may" function with a "where" gate (subsection (5)) answers JUST FALSE
-- when the gate fails, as the rulings of 2026-11-05 give; it is listed in the fork register as one of the group left for a lawyer.

§ `Section 7(4) -- Offences by Public Service employees`

-- src:496 | Offences by Public Service employees
-- src:497 | (4) Every one who, while employed as an employee within the meaning of the Public Service Employment Act in a place outside Canada, commits an act or omission in that place that is an offence under the laws of that place and that, if committed in Canada, would be an offence punishable by indictment shall be deemed to have committed that act or omission in Canada.
@ref s 7(4) (src:496-497)
GIVEN `the person is employed as an employee within the meaning of the Public Service Employment Act in a place outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or omission is committed in that place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an offence under the laws of that place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the class of offence the act or omission would be if committed in Canada` IS A `Class of offence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(4) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is employed as an employee within the meaning of the Public Service Employment Act in a place outside Canada` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "while employed as an employee within the meaning of the Public Service Employment Act in a place outside Canada"
        IF NOT `the act or omission is committed in that place` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "commits an act or omission in that place"
        IF NOT `it is an offence under the laws of that place` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that is an offence under the laws of that place"
        IF `the class of offence the act or omission would be if committed in Canada` EQUALS `an offence punishable on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "would be an offence punishable by indictment"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 7(4.1) to (4.3) -- Sexual offences against children, trafficking in persons, section 240.1; the consent of the Attorney General`

-- src:498 | Offence in relation to sexual offences against children
-- src:499 | (4.1) Despite anything in this Act or any other Act, every one who, outside Canada, commits an act or omission against a person who is under the age of 18, that, if committed in Canada, would be an offence under section 151, 152, 153 or 155, subsection 160(2) or (3), section 163.1, 170, 171, 171.1, 172.1, 172.2, 173, 271, 272 or 273 or subsection 286.1(2) shall be deemed to commit that act or omission in Canada if the person who commits the act or omission is a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act.
@ref s 7(4.1) (src:498-499)
GIVEN `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the age in years of the person against whom it is committed` IS A NUMBER
      offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the person who commits it is a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(4.1) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every one who, outside Canada, commits an act or omission"
        IF `the age in years of the person against whom it is committed` AT LEAST 18 THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "against a person who is under the age of 18"
        IF NOT `the offence is one of the listed provisions` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence under section 151, 152, 153 or 155, subsection 160(2) or (3), section 163.1, 170, 171, 171.1, 172.1, 172.2, 173, 271, 272 or 273 or subsection 286.1(2)"
        IF `the person who commits it is a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be deemed to commit that act or omission in Canada if the person who commits the act or omission is a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident"
    WHERE
        `the offence is one of the listed provisions` MEANS
            `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 151 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 152 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 153 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 155
            OR `s 7 the offence is in the subsection or paragraph` offence 160 "(2)" OR `s 7 the offence is in the subsection or paragraph` offence 160 "(3)"
            OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 163.1 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 170 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 171 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 171.1
            OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 172.1 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 172.2 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 173
            OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 271 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 272 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 273
            OR `s 7 the offence is in the subsection or paragraph` offence 286.1 "(2)"

-- src:500 | Offence in relation to trafficking in persons
-- src:501 | (4.11) Notwithstanding anything in this Act or any other Act, every one who, outside Canada, commits an act or omission that if committed in Canada would be an offence against section 279.01, 279.011, 279.02 or 279.03 shall be deemed to commit that act or omission in Canada if the person who commits the act or omission is a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act.
@ref s 7(4.11) (src:500-501)
GIVEN `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the person who commits it is a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(4.11) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every one who, outside Canada, commits an act or omission"
        IF NOT (`s 7 the offence is in section` offence 279.01 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 279.011 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 279.02 OR `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 279.03) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence against section 279.01, 279.011, 279.02 or 279.03"
        IF `the person who commits it is a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be deemed to commit that act or omission in Canada if the person who commits the act or omission is a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident"

-- src:502 | Offence outside Canada
-- src:503 | (4.2) Despite anything in this Act or any other Act, a person who commits an act or omission outside Canada that, if committed in Canada, would be an offence under section 240.1 is deemed to commit that act or omission in Canada if the person is a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act.
@ref s 7(4.2) (src:502-503)
GIVEN `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the person is a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(4.2) the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the act or omission is committed outside Canada` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person who commits an act or omission outside Canada"
        IF NOT `s 7 the offence is in section` offence 240.1 THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "would be an offence under section 240.1"
        IF `the person is a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident within the meaning of subsection 2(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is deemed to commit that act or omission in Canada if the person is a Canadian citizen or a permanent resident"

-- src:504 | Consent of Attorney General
-- src:505 | (4.3) Proceedings with respect to an act or omission deemed to have been committed in Canada under subsection (4.1) or (4.2) may only be instituted with the consent of the Attorney General.
@ref s 7(4.3) (src:504-505)
GIVEN `the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada under subsection (4.1) or (4.2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consent of the Attorney General has been obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(4.3) the proceedings are barred for want of the consent of the Attorney General` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the act or omission is deemed to have been committed in Canada under subsection (4.1) or (4.2)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Proceedings with respect to an act or omission deemed to have been committed in Canada under subsection (4.1) or (4.2)"
        IF `the consent of the Attorney General has been obtained` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may only be instituted with the consent of the Attorney General"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 7(5) to (7) -- Jurisdiction, appearance, previous trial outside Canada, consent for an accused who is not a Canadian citizen`

-- src:506 | Jurisdiction
-- src:507 | (5) Where a person is alleged to have committed an act or omission that is an offence by virtue of this section, proceedings in respect of that offence may, whether or not that person is in Canada, be commenced in any territorial division in Canada and the accused may be tried and punished in respect of that offence in the same manner as if the offence had been committed in that territorial division.
@ref s 7(5) (src:506-507)
GIVEN `the person is alleged to have committed an act or omission that is an offence by virtue of section 7` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(5) proceedings may be commenced in any territorial division in Canada, whether or not the person is in Canada` MEANS
    IF `the person is alleged to have committed an act or omission that is an offence by virtue of section 7`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is alleged to have committed an act or omission that is an offence by virtue of this section"

@ref s 7(5) (src:507-507)
GIVEN `the person is alleged to have committed an act or omission that is an offence by virtue of section 7` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(5) the accused may be tried and punished as if the offence had been committed in the territorial division` MEANS
    IF `the person is alleged to have committed an act or omission that is an offence by virtue of section 7`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is alleged to have committed an act or omission that is an offence by virtue of this section"

-- src:508 | Appearance of accused at trial
-- src:509 | (5.1) For greater certainty, the provisions of this Act relating to
-- src:510 | (a) requirements that an accused appear at and be present during proceedings, and
-- src:511 | (b) the exceptions to those requirements,
-- src:512 | apply to proceedings commenced in any territorial division pursuant to subsection (5).
@ref s 7(5.1) (src:508-512)
GIVEN `the proceedings were commenced in a territorial division in Canada pursuant to subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(5.1) the provisions relating to the accused's appearance and presence, and the exceptions, apply to the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings were commenced in a territorial division in Canada pursuant to subsection (5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "apply to proceedings commenced in any territorial division pursuant to subsection (5)"

-- src:513 | If previously tried outside Canada
-- src:514 | (6) If a person is alleged to have committed an act or omission that is an offence by virtue of this section and that person has been tried and dealt with outside Canada in respect of the offence in such a manner that, if that person had been tried and dealt with in Canada, they would be able to plead autrefois acquit,autrefois convict, pardon or an expungement order under the Expungement of Historically Unjust Convictions Act, that person shall be deemed to have been so tried and dealt with in Canada.
@ref s 7(6) (src:513-514)
GIVEN `the person is alleged to have committed an act or omission that is an offence by virtue of section 7` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been tried and dealt with outside Canada in respect of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in such a manner that, had they been tried and dealt with in Canada, they would be able to plead autrefois acquit, autrefois convict, pardon or an expungement order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(6) the person is deemed to have been tried and dealt with in Canada` MEANS
    IF `the person is alleged to have committed an act or omission that is an offence by virtue of section 7`
       AND `the person has been tried and dealt with outside Canada in respect of the offence`
       AND `in such a manner that, had they been tried and dealt with in Canada, they would be able to plead autrefois acquit, autrefois convict, pardon or an expungement order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a person is alleged to have committed an act or omission that is an offence by virtue of this section and that person has been tried and dealt with outside Canada in respect of the offence in such a manner that"

-- (7): "no proceedings ... shall be continued unless the consent of the Attorney General of Canada is obtained not later than eight days after the proceedings are commenced".
-- src:515 | If accused not Canadian citizen
-- src:516 | (7) If the accused is not a Canadian citizen, no proceedings in respect of which courts have jurisdiction by virtue of this section shall be continued unless the consent of the Attorney General of Canada is obtained not later than eight days after the proceedings are commenced.
@ref s 7(7) (src:515-516)
GIVEN `the day the proceedings were commenced` IS A DATE
`s 7(7) the last day on which the consent of the Attorney General of Canada may be obtained` MEANS `the day the proceedings were commenced` PLUS 8   -- "not later than eight days after the proceedings are commenced"

@ref s 7(7) (src:515-516)
GIVEN `the accused is not a Canadian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
      `courts have jurisdiction in the proceedings by virtue of section 7` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the proceedings were commenced` IS A DATE
      `the day the consent of the Attorney General of Canada was obtained, if it has been` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7(7) the continuation of the proceedings is barred for want of consent obtained in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `courts have jurisdiction in the proceedings by virtue of section 7` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "no proceedings in respect of which courts have jurisdiction by virtue of this section"
        IF NOT `the accused is not a Canadian citizen` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the accused is not a Canadian citizen"
        IF `the consent was obtained on or before the last day` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the consent of the Attorney General of Canada is obtained not later than eight days after the proceedings are commenced"
        IF `the consent was obtained` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the day on which the question is asked` AT MOST `s 7(7) the last day on which the consent of the Attorney General of Canada may be obtained` `the day the proceedings were commenced` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the eight days have not yet run out, and the subsection does not say what the position is while they run
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the consent was obtained` MEANS NOT (`the day the consent of the Attorney General of Canada was obtained, if it has been` EQUALS NOTHING)
        `the consent was obtained on or before the last day` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the day the consent of the Attorney General of Canada was obtained, if it has been`
            WHEN JUST d THEN d AT MOST `s 7(7) the last day on which the consent of the Attorney General of Canada may be obtained` `the day the proceedings were commenced`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
